---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/layout/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../components/sections/Prose.astro';
import { legal, entityName, entityPlace, subprocessors } from '../lib/legal';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — MindStack"
  description="What this website collects, what it does not, and who handles the data you send us."
  quiet
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy"
    lead="This site collects almost nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no third-party scripts. The only personal information we receive is what you choose to type into the contact form."
  />

  <Prose updated={legal.updated}>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {entityName} is a software team based in {entityPlace}. We design and build websites and
      applications and operate the cloud infrastructure underneath them. For anything in this
      policy, write to <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects automatically</h2>
    <p>
      In your browser, nothing. This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, runs no analytics, and
      loads no advertising, social or tracking scripts. It makes no requests to third-party domains
      at all — every asset is served from our own domain.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our host records standard server logs — IP address, timestamp, the page requested and your
      browser's user agent. Those logs exist so the site can be delivered and abuse can be
      investigated. We do not use them to build a profile of you.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you switch between light and dark mode, we save a single value in your browser's local
      storage under the key <code>ms-theme</code>, containing the word <code>light</code> or{' '}
      <code>dark</code>. Nothing is written unless you change the theme, and the value is never
      transmitted to us or to anyone else. Clearing your site data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit the form on our contact page we receive the fields you filled in: your name,
      your email address, which of web, app or infrastructure you need, an optional budget range, and
      the context you describe.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use it for one purpose: to reply to your enquiry and, if it goes further, to scope the work.
      We do not sell it, share it for marketing, or add you to a mailing list. There is no
      newsletter and no automated follow-up sequence.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
    <p>To deliver the site and your message, these services process data on our behalf:</p>
    <dl>
      {
        subprocessors.map((service) => (
          <>
            <dt>{service.name}</dt>
            <dd>
              {service.role}. {service.data}.
            </dd>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries stay in our mailbox as ordinary business correspondence, so we have a record of what
      was discussed. If an enquiry does not become a project, there is no separate system it gets
      copied into — the site itself stores nothing. Ask us to delete your enquiry and we will.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
      it. Email <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a> and we will
      respond within one business day. Because the only thing we normally hold is an email thread,
      these requests are usually quick to action.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This is a business-to-business website. It is not directed at children and we do not knowingly
      collect information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change what we collect or who processes it, we will update this page and the date at the
      top. Material changes to how we handle an existing enquiry would be raised with you directly
      rather than buried here.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
